---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import StackDiagram from "../components/StackDiagram.astro";
import TinCard from "../components/TinCard.astro";
import PerfTable from "../components/PerfTable.astro";
import { tins, tinsByTier, TIER_LABEL } from "../data/tins";
import { perfGroups, passes } from "../data/perf";
import { upstreamIssues, STATUS_LABEL } from "../data/upstream";

const description =
  "An exploration of running data workflows on Mojo: a native Apache Iceberg stack — Parquet, Avro, Thrift, codecs, Roaring bitmaps, object storage and threads — published as tins on mojoshelf and gated against the reference implementation of every format.";

const worksToday = [
  "Iceberg format v1–v3 reads, with position deletes, equality deletes and v3 deletion vectors",
  "Schema evolution and nested types through the read path",
  "Fast-append, row-level delete both copy-on-write and merge-on-read",
  "Overwrite and dynamic partition overwrite",
  "expire_snapshots",
  "Filesystem and REST catalogs",
  "Local, HTTP, S3, GCS and Azure IO",
];

const notYet = [
  "Compaction — rewrite_manifests",
  "Encryption",
  "Brotli",
  "Predicates inside list and map elements",
];

---

<Base title="Data lake building blocks in Mojo" description={description} bare={false}>
  <Hero />

  <!-- ============================ what this is ============================ -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="what">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow">What this is</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">An experiment, not a product</h2>

      <div class="two-col">
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            The question behind magmalake is narrow and answerable: <strong>can a modern
            data stack exist natively in Mojo</strong> — and what does it cost to build one?
            The formats are implemented rather than wrapped: Parquet, Avro, Thrift,
            Iceberg itself, Roaring bitmaps, Snappy and the hashes all decode bytes in
            Mojo instead of delegating. Where a mature C library is genuinely the right
            answer it is linked, not reimplemented — <strong>libzstd</strong> and
            <strong>liblz4</strong> for those two codecs, <strong>libcurl</strong> for HTTP
            and TLS, and <strong>pthreads</strong> for the threads the language does not yet
            provide. What is gone is the Python and JVM layer that every other route from
            Mojo to Iceberg has to go through.
        </p>
          <p>
            Before this, none of it existed. There was no Parquet page decode in Mojo, no
            Avro, no zstd or snappy or lz4, no Roaring bitmaps, no SHA-256, and no table
            format anywhere in the ecosystem. Every Mojo dataframe reached Parquet by calling
            through to PyArrow. So the experiment had to start at the bottom and work up.
          </p>
          <p>
            What came out is twelve tins. Some of the answers are encouraging — native
            Parquet decode is <em>faster</em> than pyarrow on a single core. Some are not:
            writes are slower, thread-pooled scans lose, and the language is still missing
            pieces a data stack assumes. Both halves are on this page, because an experiment
            you only report the wins from is not an experiment.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="callout">
          <h3 class="callout__title">Packaged on mojoshelf</h3>
          <p>
            The Mojo ecosystem is young enough that there is no established way to publish and
            consume a library, so magmalake leans on the packaging infrastructure defined by
            <a href="https://mojoshelf.org" rel="noopener">mojoshelf.org</a> — a registry for
            Mojo <em>tins</em>. Every tin here is published there and installable with one
            command.
          </p>
          <pre class="callout__code"><code>pixi shelf add iceberg-mojo</code></pre>
          <p class="callout__fine">
            Source tins are consumed as git submodules, or as pixi git source dependencies.
            Twelve packages, one registry, no vendoring.
          </p>
          <a class="callout__link" href="https://mojoshelf.org" rel="noopener">
            mojoshelf.org
            <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"
                 stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M3 9 9 3M4.2 3H9v4.8" />
            </svg>
          </a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================== the stack ============================= -->
  <section class="section" id="stack">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow">The stack</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Twelve tins, one layering</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        Iceberg sits on Parquet, Avro, Roaring and objectstore; those sit on Thrift, the
        compression codecs and the hashes; threads runs alongside all of it. Nothing is
        bundled — take the one you need.
      </p>
      <StackDiagram />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================================ tins =============================== -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="tins">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow">The tins</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">What each one is, and what proves it</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Every tin is Apache-2.0, published on mojoshelf, and CI-tested on stable Mojo 1.0.0
        and the current nightly, across macOS and Linux. Each carries its own correctness
        oracle — an outside implementation it has to agree with.
      </p>

      {
        (["table", "format", "primitive", "oracle"] as const).map((tier) => (
          <div class="tier">
            <h3 class="tier__label">{TIER_LABEL[tier]}</h3>
            <div class:list={["tin-grid", tier === "table" && "tin-grid--lead"]}>
              {tinsByTier(tier).map((t) => (
                <TinCard tin={t} featured={tier === "table"} />
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================= performance ============================ -->
  <section class="section" id="performance">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow">Performance</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Measured, including where it loses</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Apple M4, single core unless a row says otherwise. Same machine, same files,
        reproducible from each repository with <code>pixi run bench</code>. magmalake beats
        pyarrow on single-core Parquet reads; it loses on writes and on multi-threaded scans,
        where the remaining Iceberg gap is largely libzstd itself.
      </p>

      <div class="perf-groups">
        {perfGroups.map((g) => <PerfTable group={g} />)}
      </div>

      <div class="two-col two-col--wide">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3 class="panel__title">Threads, for now, come from a tin</h3>
          <p>
            Mojo's standard library currently has no threading. <code>parallelize</code> was
            removed and there is no thread pool reachable from user code, so every number
            above that mentions more than one core goes through
            <a href="https://github.com/magmalake/threads.mojo" rel="noopener">magmalake/threads</a>,
            which wraps pthreads directly via <code>external_call</code>.
          </p>
          <p>
            That tin is <strong>inspired by and distilled from
            <a href="https://github.com/ehsanmok/flare" rel="noopener">flare</a></strong>
            — Ehsan Mokhtarian's project, MIT-licensed — which worked out how to get real OS
            threads out of Mojo in the first place. threads.mojo keeps the parts a data stack
            needs and drops the rest.
          </p>
          <p class="panel__fine">
            It is explicitly a stopgap. When the language ships its own threading, this tin
            should stop existing.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="panel">
          <h3 class="panel__title">How these numbers were found</h3>
          <p class="panel__fine" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
            Four optimisation passes, each of which located its bottleneck by profiling rather
            than by guessing. None of them was where it seemed obvious to look.
          </p>
          <ol class="passes">
            {
              passes.map((p) => (
                <li>
                  <span class="passes__found">{p.found}</span>
                  <span class="passes__fix">{p.fix}</span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================= correctness ============================ -->
  <section class="section section--alt" id="correctness">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow">Correctness</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Gated on someone else's implementation</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        A format library that only passes its own tests has proved nothing. Every format tin
        here is checked against the reference implementation of the format, in both
        directions where the format has two.
      </p>

      <div class="proofs">
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>Iceberg</h3>
          <p>
            Row-sets <strong>cell-exact against PyIceberg 0.11.1 and DuckDB 1.5.5</strong>, in
            both directions, including deletes, deletion vectors and schema evolution. Tables
            magmalake writes are read back cell-exact by both — and PyIceberg can append to a
            table magmalake created.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>Parquet</h3>
          <p>
            Value-exact against pyarrow on 33 fixtures — every value of every column — and
            pyarrow reads back every file magmalake writes. The Arrow export imports through
            <code>pyarrow.Array._import_from_c</code>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>Avro &amp; Thrift</h3>
          <p>
            Avro round-trips against fastavro both ways across all four codecs. Thrift is
            <strong>byte-identical to Apache Thrift</strong> on generated wire vectors, in
            both the compact and the binary protocol.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>S3 &amp; SigV4</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>37 of 37</strong> cases of the official AWS SigV4 test suite, every stage.
            S3 is verified end-to-end against MinIO <strong>in CI</strong>, not only on a
            developer's machine.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>Roaring</h3>
          <p>
            Byte-exact against pyroaring in both directions, with pyroaring-produced payloads
            baked into the tests as constants so the oracle cannot drift.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof">
          <h3>Everything else</h3>
          <p>
            Codecs against Python <code>zstandard</code>, <code>lz4</code> and
            <code>python-snappy</code>; hashes against zlib, mmh3 and xxhash plus the Iceberg
            spec's own vectors; threads against contended-count and memory-visibility proofs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="upstream">
        <h3 class="upstream__title">Building it found bugs upstream</h3>
        <p class="upstream__blurb">
          Holding three implementations against each other surfaces disagreements, and not all
          of them were magmalake's fault. Each one below was cut down to a standalone script
          or unit test with no magmalake code in it, then either reported upstream or — where
          someone had got there first — matched to the report that already existed.
        </p>
        <ul class="upstream__list">
          {
            upstreamIssues.map((u) => (
              <li>
                <a class="upstream__head" href={u.url} rel="noopener">
                  <span class="upstream__project">{u.project}</span>
                  <span class="upstream__ref">{u.ref}</span>
                  <span class:list={["upstream__tag", `upstream__tag--${u.status}`]}>
                    {STATUS_LABEL[u.status]}
                  </span>
                </a>
                <span class="upstream__bug">{u.bug}</span>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =============================== status ============================== -->
  <section class="section" id="status">
    <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow">Status</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Active, v0.x</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Reads are complete for Iceberg format v1 through v3. Writes cover the common table
        operations. Several things are genuinely missing, and they are listed here rather
        than left to be discovered.
      </p>

      <div class="status-grid">
        <div class="status-col status-col--yes">
          <h3 class="status-col__head">Works today</h3>
          <ul>{worksToday.map((w) => <li>{w}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
        <div class="status-col status-col--no">
          <h3 class="status-col__head">Not yet</h3>
          <ul>{notYet.map((n) => <li>{n}</li>)}</ul>
          <p class="status-col__fine">
            The spec's v4 drafts — relative paths and <code>content_stats</code> — are tracked
            but not implemented.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta">
        <div>
          <h3 class="cta__title">Take a tin</h3>
          <p class="cta__text">
            Each of the {tins.length} repositories is independently usable and independently
            installable. Start with whichever layer you need.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="cta__actions">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="https://github.com/magmalake" rel="noopener">
            github.com/magmalake
          </a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://mojoshelf.org" rel="noopener">mojoshelf.org</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ---- shared section furniture ---- */
  .two-col {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .two-col--wide {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .two-col,
    .two-col--wide {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2.25rem;
    }
  }

  /* ---- mojoshelf callout ---- */
  .callout {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--lake);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .callout__title {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }
  .callout p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .callout__code {
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .callout__code code {
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--lake);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .callout__fine {
    font-size: 0.8125rem !important;
    color: var(--text-faint) !important;
  }
  .callout__link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.3rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .callout__link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  /* ---- tins ---- */
  .tier { margin-top: 2.75rem; }

  .tier__label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.6rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .tin-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 310px), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  /* iceberg is the only tin in its tier; give it the full width. */
  .tin-grid--lead { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }

  /* ---- performance ---- */
  .perf-groups { margin-top: 2.5rem; }

  .panel {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.6rem 1.7rem;
  }
  .panel__title {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }
  .panel p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.62;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }
  .panel__fine {
    font-size: 0.8125rem !important;
    color: var(--text-faint) !important;
  }

  .passes {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: pass;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.95rem;
  }
  .passes li {
    counter-increment: pass;
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 2rem;
  }
  .passes li::before {
    content: counter(pass);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.05em;
    width: 1.35rem;
    height: 1.35rem;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ember-wash);
    color: var(--ember);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .passes__found {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .passes__fix {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
  }

  /* ---- correctness ---- */
  .proofs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 290px), 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    background: var(--border);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .proof {
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .proof h3 {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--lake);
  }
  .proof p {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .proof strong { color: var(--text); }

  .upstream {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember) 28%, var(--border));
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--ember-wash);
    padding: 1.6rem 1.7rem;
  }
  .upstream__title {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
  }
  .upstream__blurb {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
  .upstream__list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 240px), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .upstream__list li {
    border-left: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember) 45%, transparent);
    padding-left: 0.85rem;
  }
  .upstream__head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 0.55rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .upstream__head:hover .upstream__ref { text-decoration: underline; }
  .upstream__project {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ember);
  }
  .upstream__ref {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .upstream__tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    color: var(--text-faint);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .upstream__tag--filed {
    color: var(--ember);
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember) 45%, transparent);
  }
  .upstream__bug {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* ---- status ---- */
  .status-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.25fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .status-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  .status-col {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.5rem 1.6rem;
  }
  .status-col__head {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.7rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .status-col--yes .status-col__head { color: var(--lake); }
  .status-col--no .status-col__head { color: var(--ember); }

  .status-col ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }
  .status-col li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .status-col li::before {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }
  .status-col--yes li::before { content: "+"; color: var(--lake); }
  .status-col--no li::before { content: "\2013"; color: var(--ember); }

  .status-col__fine {
    margin: 1.1rem 0 0;
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  /* ---- closing CTA ---- */
  .cta {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: linear-gradient(
      120deg,
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--ember) 7%, var(--surface)),
      color-mix(in srgb, var(--lake) 7%, var(--surface))
    );
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .cta__title { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .cta__text {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 48ch;
  }
  .cta__actions { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  .btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.65rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.15s ease;
  }
  .btn:hover { border-color: var(--text-muted); box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .btn--primary {
    background: var(--ember);
    border-color: var(--ember);
    color: #fff;
  }
  :root[data-theme="dark"] .btn--primary { color: #1a0d06; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) .btn--primary { color: #1a0d06; }
  }
  .btn--primary:hover {
    background: var(--ember-soft);
    border-color: var(--ember-soft);
  }
</style>
